E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:25:30-32 malformed-format-string "this `{` is never closed" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"close the hole with `}`, or write `{{` for a literal brace"
E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:29:27-28 malformed-format-string "this `}` closes a hole that was never opened" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"write `}}` for a literal closing brace"
E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:33:27-28 malformed-format-string "an empty hole `{}` names nothing to interpolate" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"a hole names a binding in scope at the CALL - `{count}` interpolates `count`. There are no positional arguments and no argument list: write the name in the string, or `{{` for a literal brace"
E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:37:30-31 malformed-format-string "this `{` opens a hole that does not name a binding" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"a hole names a binding in scope at the CALL - `{count}` interpolates `count`. There are no positional arguments and no argument list: write the name in the string, or `{{` for a literal brace"
E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:41:38-40 malformed-format-string "this hole is not closed: ` ` is neither `}` nor `:`" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"a hole is `{name}`, or `{name:SPEC}` with a format specifier - `{n:>8}`, `{x:.2}`, `{n:04x}`"
E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:45:38-43 malformed-format-string "this `{` is never closed" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"close the hole with `}` after its format specifier"
E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:49:36-37 malformed-format-string "`q` is not a format-specifier type" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"the types are `x` and `X`, both hexadecimal. Alignment and width come first (`{n:>8x}`) and a precision is `.N` (`{x:.2}`)"
E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:53:47-48 malformed-format-string "a `.` in a format specifier needs a digit count after it" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"write `{x:.2}` for two decimal places"
E AX3031 570-format-refusals.ax:59:39-41 malformed-format-string "this is left over after the format specifier" !"a format string is parsed at expansion time, so every hole in it is checked before the program runs; `{{` and `}}` write a literal brace" ?"a specifier is [align][0][width][.precision][type], in that order - `{x:>08.2}`"
